The cleaned NumPy implementation extracts the selected spherical numerical
branch, with explicitly documented V2 light travel corrections, instead of
bundling the original general stellar-shape framework or compiled library.
The task-specific initializer, ensemble updates, tests, and review materials
are supplied under the same license.

The real J0113+31 observations are the original example's copies of tables
5–10 accompanying Gómez Maqueo Chew et al., Astronomy & Astrophysics 572,
A50 (2014), DOI 10.1051/0004-6361/201424265. Their authors and publication
retain the observational attribution; the benchmark does not assert ownership
of the original astronomical measurements. The package preserves full supplied
decimal observation values, with the separate source likelihood precision
convention explicitly documented.
